Sometimes bags of tricks do this.  They're tricky things (ho ho). 
Seriously, about one out of every ten applications (approximate values,
I haven't looked at the source, so this is just my observation) results
in an effect similar to reading a cursed scroll of create monster:  a
huge army surrounding you.

> Also is there some generic way of getting out of trouble when 
> you get surrounded by a big number in the middle of a room.

Well, the first and most obvious thing you can do is teleport.  Any
scrolls of teleportation or wands of teleportation should be used pronto
if you don't think you can handle the mob.  Beyond this solution, there
are a couple of things you can do.

First, if you have any rings of conflict, put 'em on.  That'll help alot
(prior to 3.1, it would completely solve your problems).  Become
invisible if at all possible, as this will increase your life
expectancy.  Should you happen to have any cursed potions of gain level
(and we all know how common THOSE are), you could quaff those and more
up a level.  There are a few things you can do if you're going to stand
your ground and fight like a man.

First, unless you already have double speed, quaff a potion of speed. 
Next, see if there is a corner nearby.  If there is, go for it, to the
point of using all available wands to go for the corner.  Once installed
there, use any remaining wands to blast quantities of monsters.  Careful
about bounces, though.  Always fight the monster with the most damage
potential first.  That means go for "q"s before attacking those molds. 
Nail spellcasters at the start as getting stunned is no fun when you're
surrounded.  Concentrate your attacks on one monster...scattering your
attacks is a recipe for death.  Don't forget to pray when you're low on
hit points as this second wind can often be enough to pull out a
victory.  Plus, sacrificing all those fresh corpses would probably
reconcile you with your god afterwards.  Don't forget that you can throw
potions of sickness, blindness, paralysis and confusion at monsters. 
Should you happen to have an expensive camera handy, use it as this can
sometimes cause monsters to attack other monsters (or just go staggering
off).  Above all, don't give up.  A true hacker goes down swingin'.  :)

